  ;; --- C19: stage 2 of create-record-type as a graph `:cond`. Was a
  ;; Clojure base-fn delegating to a since-removed
  ;; `validate-create-record-type` helper; now decomposed into per-field
  ;; extractors + predicates + static
  ;; error responses, glued by a flat `:cond`. The 400-rejection
  ;; literals live in `:_create-record-type-err-*` consts (skill §4
  ;; "Content → fn-defs, not impls"). The `:cond` is lazy, so each
  ;; predicate's `:_create-record-type-parsed` lookup runs at most once
  ;; per call (shared via the cond's `:parsed` bind). ---

  {:name :_create-record-type-parsed-name
   :description "Pull the `:name` field out of `:_create-record-type-parsed`'s output. Shared by the blank-name guard and (potentially) the success response."
